&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;With over 50 nationalities represented, we’re proud to welcome people of all backgrounds to our growing community, and we’re always finding new ways to help people feel welcomed and included. Here, you’ll have the tools, training and support you need to work in a way that suits you, learn new skills and reach your potential.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;For a career where you can drive our business and shape your future, apply now.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Location&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;: Come and join us in Berlin!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Freenow by Lyft empowers smarter mobility decisions helping people to move freely and cities to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced Engineering Manager to lead two high-performing teams of software engineers who are focused on scaling an exciting new product vertical. We are building a complex, intelligent system to modernize the traditional taxi industry. Your goal is to lead the team to transform offline fleets into digital businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This critical role ensures team’s alignment with product and business strategy, while driving efficient delivery of features. You will foster an environment of technical excellence, psychological safety, and continuous individual development, ultimately maximizing business impact across all Freenow markets through innovation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Be ready to work in a multinational, diverse, highly motivated and collaborative team of passionate colleagues who strive for excellence and enjoy their work. Are you ready for your next ride?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR DAILY ADVENTURES WILL INCLUDE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Performance &amp;amp; Delivery:&lt;/strong&gt; Within the frame of quarterly goals and company strategy, lead the team in delivering high-quality, scalable software solutions. Focus on continuously improving engineering processes to ensure predictable, timely delivery while managing team capacity and focus. You inspire innovation to disrupt incumbents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide coaching, mentoring, and continuous feedback to team members. Identify development areas and growth opportunities to support individual career paths and enhance team cohesion in building innovative customer and driver support solutions. You get to build a team from the ground up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; In collaboration with Staff Engineers and Principals, lead technical decision-making for the support systems. Ensure high standards of quality, reliability, maintainability, and observability in all solutions, particularly the large-scale systems handling customer and driver interactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Translate product and tech strategy into actionable team plans. Align team activities with business priorities, ensuring efficient execution and adapting plans as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the main engineering counterpart to Product Managers and Designers. Build strong relationships to ensure transparency, collaborate on product decisions where needed, and jointly maximize business impact by providing world-class support technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture &amp;amp; Team Building:&lt;/strong&gt; Foster a team culture based on trust, psychological safety, collaboration, and feedback. Ensure diverse perspectives are heard, encourage curiosity, and build a resilient and motivated team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence &amp;amp; Incident Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Own incident response processes for support technology. Ensure alerting and monitoring are in place, bugs are addressed quickly, and technical debt is managed proactively to support long-term sustainability and reliability of the critical customer and driver support infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Techstack&lt;/strong&gt;: Java | Kotlin | AWS | Docker | Git | Kafka | ElasticSearch &amp;amp; &lt;a href=&quot;https://stackshare.io/free-now&quot;&gt;more&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TO BE SUCCESSFUL IN THIS ROLE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Level of Education: Bachelor&#39;s degree (preferably in Computer Science or a related technical field).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Level of relevant working experience: Minimum 6 years in software engineering roles, and at least 2 years in a leadership or management position.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the software development lifecycle and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with scaling zero to one products&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership, coaching, and people development skills.&lt;/li&gt;
